{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Our leaders</b> — like 'your cattle-bearing young' (Deuteronomy 7:13), and similar to it 'a chosen lamb' (Isaiah 30:24)." "<b>Loaded</b> — for they bear the full carts." "<b>There is no breach</b> — in the city walls." "<b>And none go out</b> — through the great, known gates." "<b>And no outcry in our streets</b> — for such was their custom when evil tidings came, that Israel was struck down before its enemies."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 144, :notes {0 "The Hebrew word אלופינו is glossed by analogy to words sharing the root א-ל-ף; the translated lemma reflects Ibn Ezra's reading of the term as referring to flocks/herds rather than human chieftains."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:46.242141348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}